; A `year` directive names the year for dates written without one; it
; must not change what "now" is.  xact and template hide the directive
; while drafting so the new transaction is dated against --now (#707),
; but they used to also discard --now whenever it fell on December 31
; of the directive's year, guessing that the year directive had set it,
; and drafted against the wall clock instead.

year 2024

01/05 Grocer
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test --now 2024/12/31 xact 03/20 Grocer
2024/03/20 Grocer
    Expenses:Food                             $10.00
    Assets:Cash
end test

test --now 2024/12/31 xact today Grocer
2024/12/31 Grocer
    Expenses:Food                             $10.00
    Assets:Cash
end test

test --now 2024/12/31 xact Grocer
2024/12/31 Grocer
    Expenses:Food                             $10.00
    Assets:Cash
end test

test --now 2024/12/30 xact 03/20 Grocer
2024/03/20 Grocer
    Expenses:Food                             $10.00
    Assets:Cash
end test
